WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:29.920
Gemini 4 Carbon scores 88.2% on vulnerability finding and leads the artificial analysis intelligence index at 59. This is Models &amp; Agents, episode 218. Open Speech Models, a frozen agent adapter and community coding skills follow. Then things to try. Google DeepMind announced Gemini 4 Carbon on its blog as the second model in the Gemini 4 family after Argon two weeks earlier. Carbon posts 54.8% on exploit gym

00:00:29.920 --> 00:00:34.620
for exploitation, and 71% on CWE bench for patching.

00:00:35.060 --> 00:00:40.360
Internal tests show secure code generation improved more than twofold over argon, with

00:00:40.360 --> 00:00:44.840
reduced misalignment and fabrication rates in live coding environments used by Google

00:00:44.840 --> 00:00:45.240
Teams.

00:00:45.920 --> 00:00:50.900
The model targets sustained, agentic workflows that can run for days on complex engineering

00:00:50.900 --> 00:00:54.820
tasks, such as root causing bugs across large code bases.

00:00:54.820 --> 00:01:00.540
Access begins this week with a subset of trusted cyber defenders via the Fairwind program

00:01:00.540 --> 00:01:02.960
before wider developer availability.

00:01:03.680 --> 00:01:09.400
Pricing matches are gone at $2 per million input tokens and $10 per million output tokens

00:01:09.400 --> 00:01:12.400
with cashed input at 95% off.

00:01:13.214 --> 00:01:19.594
Forty languages of speech now go through Nemotron 3.5 Transcribe, an open-weight speech-large

00:01:19.594 --> 00:01:26.974
language model or LLM, Nvidia released, 4.3 billion active parameters sit inside a 30 billion

00:01:26.974 --> 00:01:33.774
mixture of experts or MOE architecture, MarkTech post reports, speaker labels and word time stamps

00:01:33.774 --> 00:01:39.614
come with the transcripts, mean word error rate or WER on the English open automatic speech

00:01:39.614 --> 00:01:49.370
recognition or ASR leaderboard is 4.71 percent. Assembly AI released assembly AI-TTS-1, its first

00:01:49.370 --> 00:01:55.670
text-to-speech or TTS model aimed at voice agents. It costs $15 per million characters.

00:01:56.290 --> 00:02:01.110
Unlimited concurrency is supported without a contract. The launch covers six languages.

00:02:02.255 --> 00:02:08.375
On a MacBook Pro M4 Max, Bloc's full duplex speech-to-speech model, Dessa, now runs locally.

00:02:09.035 --> 00:02:15.195
Bloc's AI lab trained Dessa solely on human conversation audio, so it learns from talking rather than

00:02:15.195 --> 00:02:15.715
from text.

00:02:16.713 --> 00:02:20.213
Meastral Large-4 fell from rank 38 to rank 25

00:02:20.213 --> 00:02:24.013
on that same updated version 5.0 Artificial Analysis

00:02:24.013 --> 00:02:24.513
Index.

00:02:25.133 --> 00:02:26.173
Actualy reports.

00:02:26.833 --> 00:02:28.433
The benchmark added harder questions

00:02:28.433 --> 00:02:30.053
and removed saturated ones.

00:02:31.058 --> 00:02:35.018
Infinity AI Lab released Hermit version 0.1.0

00:02:35.018 --> 00:02:38.098
and Apache 2.0 harness adapter framework

00:02:38.098 --> 00:02:39.418
Mark Tech Post covers.

00:02:39.998 --> 00:02:42.958
An external layer of instructions, skills, memory,

00:02:43.258 --> 00:02:45.078
and tools trains from task feedback

00:02:45.078 --> 00:02:47.918
while the agent's model and harness stay frozen.

00:02:48.438 --> 00:02:53.718
The adapter supports five evolution methods including JEPA, SkillOpt, and MetaWorld model.

00:02:54.198 --> 00:03:01.478
It runs on any API backend, or local VLLM, SGLANG, or Olama server, and the offline quickstart

00:03:01.478 --> 00:03:02.678
requires no GPU.

00:03:03.378 --> 00:03:05.938
It ships as PIP install, Hermit, HIF, and Harness.

00:03:06.438 --> 00:03:10.098
Every adapter version lands in a Git tree for inspection and rollback.

00:03:10.098 --> 00:03:15.593
COFORGE launched the Autonomous Software Factory Service, Equity Pandate Reports,

00:03:16.313 --> 00:03:20.813
specialized AI agents write, test, review, and quality check code under human

00:03:20.813 --> 00:03:25.673
supervision inside secure enterprise systems. The offering targets the post-coding

00:03:25.673 --> 00:03:30.053
era by enforcing rules and sign-off gates from the start, rather than bolting

00:03:30.053 --> 00:03:36.467
governance on later. Beyond trust phantom labs found AI coding agents generated 1.28

00:03:36.467 --> 00:03:42.447
million shell commands from 132,000 prompts over four weeks. Intelligence Cecil reports.

00:03:43.147 --> 00:03:49.047
That average is nearly 10 commands per prompt. Among users with coding agents, 85% had at least

00:03:49.047 --> 00:03:56.727
one model context protocol or MCP server connection. Connected users averaged 4.35 unique servers.

00:03:57.307 --> 00:04:04.062
One user reached 36. Managed service providers must now track agent identity and lifecycle events,

00:04:04.062 --> 00:04:05.462
IT Pro reports.

00:04:06.042 --> 00:04:10.462
Agents inherit creator permissions and retain access after the human changes roles.

00:04:11.062 --> 00:04:15.802
Security researchers showed GitHub agent workflows could be manipulated to pull data from

00:04:15.802 --> 00:04:21.302
private repositories and publish it publicly when an agent had access to both untrusted input

00:04:21.302 --> 00:04:22.622
and protected systems.

00:04:23.567 --> 00:04:28.827
Minimax open sourced M code stack under the MIT license, Marktech Post reports.

00:04:29.407 --> 00:04:33.207
The drop includes 17 skill markdown files and five checklists.

00:04:33.207 --> 00:04:39.367
Minimax's internal coding team uses them for code review, sub-agent coordination, context

00:04:39.367 --> 00:04:41.707
budgeting, and long-running command handling.

00:04:42.635 --> 00:04:46.815
Researchers on the machine learning sub-reddit showed a fixed generic feedback line can

00:04:46.815 --> 00:04:52.695
replace a model-generated critique during hindsight self-distillation on GPT OSS 20 billion.

00:04:53.435 --> 00:04:57.815
Gain stayed nearly identical at about three points on multi-step financial reasoning.

00:04:57.815 --> 00:05:03.255
The generic line used 9.5% fewer tokens than full-reference solutions.

00:05:03.635 --> 00:05:07.455
The result is headed to ACM ICAIF 2026.

00:05:08.637 --> 00:05:14.077
Injecting principal component analysis or PCA, reduced features from conformer layers

00:05:14.077 --> 00:05:20.517
2 and 6 raised embedding Gemma 2 on the MAEB audio benchmark from rank 26 to rank 1.

00:05:20.517 --> 00:05:29.077
The 577 million parameter models macro score moved from 49.3% to 54.4%.

00:05:29.077 --> 00:05:33.237
The change took zero additional training and left all text embeddings unchanged.

00:05:34.296 --> 00:05:40.756
A developer shared a three-stage continued pre-training run on Quinn 3.59B base using

00:05:40.756 --> 00:05:46.336
240 million tokens of Polish legal commentaries, legislation, and court decisions.

00:05:46.336 --> 00:05:52.936
The post asked for ordering advice on subsequent supervised fine-tuning, or SFT, for reasoning

00:05:52.936 --> 00:05:56.656
and in-harness tool use before reinforcement learning or RL.

00:05:57.702 --> 00:06:03.202
In brief, researchers told Reuters a Chinese AI model executed multi-stage cyberattacks

00:06:03.202 --> 00:06:07.902
including reconnaissance, exploitation, and persistence in controlled environments.

00:06:08.502 --> 00:06:14.262
Commodity Futures Trading Commission, or CFTC, Commissioner Christy Goldsmith Romero warned

00:06:14.262 --> 00:06:19.522
that autonomous AI agents may soon execute crypto trades without human oversight and

00:06:19.522 --> 00:06:22.202
propose new, know-your-agent compliance requirements.

00:06:22.902 --> 00:06:28.822
IIT Delhi announced an executive certificate program covering agentic AI systems, including

00:06:28.822 --> 00:06:32.662
curriculum details and eligibility criteria for working professionals.

00:06:33.342 --> 00:06:39.542
Quake AI positioned its GPU infrastructure offering around AI agents as the primary workload rather

00:06:39.542 --> 00:06:42.202
than human developers or traditional training jobs.

00:06:42.202 --> 00:06:47.527
Install hermit with PIP install hermit harness and run the offline quick start.

00:06:47.927 --> 00:06:53.347
Evolve a small adapter on Office QA or CL bench without touching your base model or harness.

00:06:53.887 --> 00:06:59.767
If your voice agents already sit on assembly AI transcription, test assembly AI TTS-1 for

00:06:59.767 --> 00:07:03.827
unlimited concurrency spoken output at $15 per million characters.

00:07:04.387 --> 00:07:11.007
Compare Nemotron 3.5 transcribe against your current ASR pipeline on the English Open ASR leaderboard.

00:07:11.007 --> 00:07:15.907
Watch the Fairwind program if your work involves vulnerability detection or long

00:07:15.907 --> 00:07:20.765
horizon agentic coding. More details on Meastrol's response to the new

00:07:20.765 --> 00:07:25.425
artificial analysis index ranking are expected in the coming weeks. Additional

00:07:25.425 --> 00:07:29.745
open source releases from Minimax on agent skills and coordination patterns are

00:07:29.745 --> 00:07:41.325
anticipated following the M code stack drop. IIT Delhi's Executive Certificate in

00:07:41.325 --> 00:07:46.145
2012 projection is the place to pop the hood on how audio can join a text embedding without

00:07:46.145 --> 00:07:47.265
a retraining pass.

00:07:47.875 --> 00:07:52.345
Adding acoustic or parallel linguistic features to a text aligned embedding model normally

00:07:52.345 --> 00:07:56.225
requires retraining or risks destroying the original text geometry.

00:07:57.115 --> 00:08:02.545
Embedding Gemma 2 leaves a 256-dimensional null space after that final projection matrix

00:08:02.545 --> 00:08:06.845
because every text vector lives inside a 512-dimensional subspace.

00:08:06.845 --> 00:08:13.085
Researcher's projected intermediate conformer layer activations down to 256 dimensions with

00:08:13.085 --> 00:08:17.325
a fit on external audio and added those directions before normalization.

00:08:17.865 --> 00:08:21.725
The injected vectors sit exactly orthogonal to all text directions.

00:08:22.325 --> 00:08:28.185
Text to text and text to audio retrieval scores remain unchanged to within 0.05 points.

00:08:28.805 --> 00:08:33.385
Audio-only tasks such as gender clustering and emotion classification rise sharply.

00:08:33.385 --> 00:08:38.245
The method works only because the final linear layer has no activation after it.

00:08:38.745 --> 00:08:41.245
Any non-linearity would mix the subspaces.

00:08:41.785 --> 00:08:46.905
Quality on spoken intent tasks drops because the added acoustic dimensions slightly dilute

00:08:46.905 --> 00:08:49.585
the semantic component after L2 normalization.

00:08:50.305 --> 00:08:55.145
Use the injection when that final layer is linear and unused orthogonal dimensions exist.

00:08:55.765 --> 00:09:00.405
Skip it when a non-linearity would mix subspaces or those dimensions are already filled.

00:09:00.405 --> 00:09:04.905
build, because the added features will leak into the text subspace and degrade retrieval.

